BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When to Pause AI?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T160000
UID:evt-dqHxGHHOH9n1UEq@events.lu.ma
DESCRIPTION:Address:\nMaRS Discovery District\nEnter the Mars Atrium via U
 niversity Avenue entrance. We'll meet at the food court in the basement. S
 ean will be wearing a bright neon yellow jacket.\nToronto\, ON\nCanada\n\n
 There is a race to develop Artificial Super Intelligence (ASI)\, an AI tha
 t can learn and execute any task better than a human can\, as soon as poss
 ible with minimal consideration for safety. Some people\, such as Pause AI
 \, think the risks of this current approach outweigh the potential benefit
 s. Assuming it were possible to adopt/enforce a Pause\, when would you pus
 h the Pause button? What capabilities of AI systems would need to be demon
 strated to convince you a catastrophic outcome was likely\, and arriving s
 oon enough\, to merit pausing?\nLets get together to read + discuss. No ne
 ed to read…\n\nHosted by Sean Aubin & Abi ☀️☀️☀️
LOCATION:MaRS Discovery District\, 101 College St\, Toronto\, ON M5G 0A3\,
  Canada
URL:https://luma.com/wz1z2snk
X-SOURCE:Luma Toronto Discover
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Home-cooked Software Meetup
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T203000
UID:evt-WKbZZpAu2o5uh4q@events.lu.ma
DESCRIPTION:Address:\n1RG\nToronto\, ON\nCanada\n\nLots of software we use
  these days feels like a fast-food restaurant: made by huge multinational 
 corporations\, designed to appeal to anyone\, optimized for quick dopamine
  hits.\nIt's easy to fall into the mindset that something’s not worth do
 ing unless it can be a huge business. Will it scale? Will it monetize?\nIt
  doesn't have to be that way — software can be a home-cooked meal\, sha
 red with only friends and family. It can be an art\, a gift for the people
  we love. What kind of software feels like having friends over for some ni
 ce soup?\nInspired by Robin Sloan’s essay and Maggie Appleton's…\n\nHo
 sted by garry ing\, Ross Zurowski & Team 1RG
LOCATION:1RG\, 2567 Dundas St W\, Toronto\, ON M6P 1X7\, Canada
URL:https://luma.com/1yd9a3gb
X-SOURCE:Luma Toronto Discover
END:VEVENT
